diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index f90dd54e..82bf35b9 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -205,6 +205,21 @@ requests without tokens.
 The executable running on the host runs a virtual gateway that can be used by the VM.
 It runs a DHCP server. It allows VMs to configure the network automatically (IP, MTU, DNS, search domain, etc.).
 
+### Outbound deny list
+
+`--outbound-deny` (repeatable, or separated by commas) lists destinations that no TCP connection,
+UDP datagram or ping of the VM may reach. Each entry is an address, a CIDR, or one of:
+
+- `private`: loopback, RFC 1918, carrier-grade NAT, link-local, multicast and reserved networks;
+- `host`: the host's own addresses;
+- `host-networks`: every network the host is attached to, which `private` misses when a local
+  network uses public addresses or global IPv6;
+- `all`: everything.
+
+For example, `--outbound-deny private,host,host-networks` lets the VM reach the internet but not
+the host nor its local network. It is checked on the address gvproxy dials, after NAT, so
+192.168.127.254 is refused through its loopback target. Forwards into the VM are not affected.
+
 ### DNS
 
 The gateway also runs a DNS server. It can be configured to serve static zones.
